         to /MT and the mismatch fails the link with LNK2038.
         zluxDOF is distributed publicly, so the kernel ships as a fat binary
         covering every architecture CUDA 13.x supports:
           sm_75  Turing    RTX 20xx, GTX 16xx
           sm_80  Ampere    A100
           sm_86  Ampere    RTX 30xx
           sm_89  Ada       RTX 40xx
           sm_90  Hopper    H100
           sm_120 Blackwell RTX 50xx
         Plus compute_120 PTX so future architectures JIT rather than falling
         back to the CPU. CUDA 13 cannot target anything below sm_75, so Pascal
         (GTX 10xx) users get the CPU path; moving to CUDA 12.9 would cover them. -->
    <CustomBuild Include="..\zluxDOF_Kernel.cu">
      <FileType>Document</FileType>
      <!-- Build against CUDA 12.9. CUDA 13 CANNOT be used here: its runtime
           initialises through a "hybrid runtime loader" (nvcudart_hybrid64.dll
           from the driver store) which access-violates on the very first
           cudaGetDeviceCount inside After Effects, where cudart64_110.dll,
           nvcuda.dll and REDCuda-x64.dll are already loaded. Confirmed from an
           AE minidump: read of 0x0 in MSVCP140, stack RunGather to Ctx() magic
           static to initializeLoader to initializeHybridRuntimeLoaderOnce to
           cudaGetDeviceCount. And there is no escape inside CUDA 13: dumpbin
           shows both cudart.lib and cudart_static.lib carry that loader and
           neither carries __imp_ stubs, so "cudart shared" changes nothing.

           CUDA 12.9's cudart.lib is a real import library for cudart64_12.dll,
           which build.bat copies next to AfterFX.exe (a plug-in's own folder is
           not on the DLL search path).

           Architectures: 12.9 reaches back to sm_50, so the freeware build
           covers Maxwell through Blackwell, plus compute_120 PTX so future
           cards JIT rather than falling back to the CPU.
             sm_50/52 Maxwell   GTX 9xx
             sm_60/61 Pascal    GTX 10xx
             sm_70    Volta     Titan V
             sm_75    Turing    RTX 20xx, GTX 16xx
             sm_80/86 Ampere    A100, RTX 30xx
             sm_89    Ada       RTX 40xx
             sm_90    Hopper    H100
             sm_120   Blackwell RTX 50xx -->
      <Command>"$(CUDA_SDK_BASE_PATH)\bin\nvcc.exe" -c "%(FullPath)" -o "$(IntDir)zluxDOF_Kernel.obj" --use-local-env -O3 -m64 -std=c++17 -cudart shared -gencode arch=compute_50,code=sm_50 -gencode arch=compute_52,code=sm_52 -gencode arch=compute_60,code=sm_60 -gencode arch=compute_61,code=sm_61 -gencode arch=compute_70,code=sm_70 -gencode arch=compute_75,code=sm_75 -gencode arch=compute_80,code=sm_80 -gencode arch=compute_86,code=sm_86 -gencode arch=compute_89,code=sm_89 -gencode arch=compute_90,code=sm_90 -gencode arch=compute_120,code=sm_120 -gencode arch=compute_120,code=compute_120 -Xcompiler /MT</Command>
      <Outputs>$(IntDir)zluxDOF_Kernel.obj</Outputs>
      <Message>nvcc zluxDOF_Kernel.cu (sm_120)</Message>
    </CustomBuild>
  </ItemGroup>
